cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Causal-axis JEPAs on prediction-market strike ladders: a negative
  result and the diagnostics that failed to predict it
message: "If you reference this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: Physical Reasoning
repository-code: "https://github.com/physicalreasoning/causal-jepa"
license: Apache-2.0
date-released: "2026-08-11"
keywords:
  - joint-embedding predictive architecture
  - self-supervised learning
  - representation collapse
  - prediction markets
  - negative results
abstract: >-
  A joint-embedding predictive architecture trained on prediction-market
  strike ladders does not learn a representation that beats raw features.
  Four pre-registered explanations were tested; three were refuted. The
  copy-alignment diagnostic built to detect martingale collapse is sound,
  is manipulable by a single hyperparameter, and does not predict
  downstream utility: over a 0.198 range of copy alignment its correlation
  with probe R-squared is +0.390, the wrong sign. Thirty-two times the
  training compute drives the nonlinear probe 23 pooled standard
  deviations below an untrained encoder of the same architecture while
  effective rank nearly triples. The headline metric was found to be
  largely measuring input reconstruction.
